    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Number of women and other vulnerable individuals achieved 20% increase in monthly income</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Recognizing the socioeconomic barriers that hinder access to justice and reintegration, the project will integrate economic empowerment into its case management approach. Targeted support will be provided to women detainees, GBV survivors, persons with disabilities (PwDs), and other vulnerable groups through vocational training, project management coaching, livelihood toolkits, and micro-grant funding. This holistic support across legal and economic empowerment aims to enhance long-term resilience, promote self-reliance, and address the underlying drivers of exclusion and repeated vulnerability.</narrative>
    </description>
